{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And I will make you a great nation, etc.</b> He blessed him here with seven blessings, and they are these: \"And I will make you a great nation\" — this is the greatest of them all, that He make him into a nation, for with this the servitude and the redemption are included. The second — while he was still Abram, before He brought him into the covenant, He blessed him with a blessing of wealth, as stated: \"And Abram was very heavy [rich]\" (Genesis 13:2). The third — that His name be magnified from Abram to Abraham. The fourth — that he himself be a blessing. The fifth — that HaShem be blessed by those who bless him. The sixth — that He curse all who seek his harm. The seventh — that all the families of the earth be blessed through him." "<b>which I will show you</b> Two times in the Masorah: here and the other in Zechariah, regarding the exiles. This teaches that the Holy One, blessed be He, showed Abraham the exiles." "<b>I will show you</b> — gematria: בעננים (with clouds). This teaches that clouds would go before him and show him the way. \"And I will make you a great nation, and I will bless you, and I will magnify your name\" — three blessings corresponding to the three blessings of the priests. And likewise מברכך — three tags on the ך, to tell you that כ three times equals 60, corresponding to the 60 letters in the priestly blessing, which are: יברכך יאר ישא. And ואברכך, in gematria: אברהם." "<b>and you shall be</b> Six times in the Masorah: והיה ברכה. והיה תמים. והיה נכון לבקר. עלה אלי ההרה והיה שם. והיה לי לאב. והיה לנו לאב. If you will be תמים and נכון, then you will be ברכה — עלה אלי ההרה והיה לי לאב."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:16:03.951297844Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}